1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,949
这个教程要问语言模型一个问题：Tolminc 奶酪是怎么做的？
Here's the question this tutorial asks a language model: how is Tolminc cheese made?

2
00:00:05,269 --> 00:00:07,504
Tolminc 是一种真实的阿尔卑斯奶酪
Tolminc is a real Alpine cheese,

3
00:00:07,504 --> 00:00:11,136
但我们要的答案在某一篇特定的文本里
but the answer we want lives in one particular text.

4
00:00:11,383 --> 00:00:13,680
知识库一共是 11 本书
The knowledge base is eleven books:

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,568
10 本 Project Gutenberg 上讲奶酪的老书
ten old cheese books from Project Gutenberg,

6
00:00:16,568 --> 00:00:19,916
加上授课老师写的一个短篇故事，一个虚构的故事
and the instructor's short story, a fictional tale.

7
00:00:20,236 --> 00:00:25,975
在这个故事出现之前训练的模型从没读过它，所以它的回答来自别处
A model trained before that story existed has never read it, so it answers from somewhere else.

8
00:00:26,295 --> 00:00:29,730
怎样让它根据这个故事回答，又不用重新训练？
How do we make it answer from this story, without retraining it?

9
00:00:29,967 --> 00:00:32,274
课上列出了四个弱点
The lecture lists four weaknesses:

10
00:00:32,274 --> 00:00:37,498
训练数据过时、缺少专业知识、幻觉，以及没有出处
stale training data, no specialized knowledge, hallucination, and no sources.

11
00:00:37,818 --> 00:00:42,063
RAG，也就是检索增强生成，针对的是前两个
RAG, retrieval augmented generation, goes after the first two.

12
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,820
把 11 本书全贴进 prompt，得到的是一堆垃圾
Paste all eleven books into the prompt, and you get garbage.

13
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:49,383
微调模型呢，又很慢；那是第 8 讲的内容
Fine-tune the model, and it's slow; that's lecture 8.

14
00:00:49,703 --> 00:00:55,079
或者让一位图书管理员，把最相关的 10 页递给它：一场开卷考试
Or let a librarian hand it the ten most relevant pages: an open-book exam.

15
00:00:55,399 --> 00:00:56,617
这就是 RAG
That's RAG.

16
00:00:56,667 --> 00:01:01,424
课上那张 RAG 技术全景图很拥挤，但它是从四个问题出发的
The lecture's map of RAG techniques is crowded, but it starts from four questions.

17
00:01:01,744 --> 00:01:05,563
什么是 embedding、向量数据库、查询，以及上下文？
What is an embedding, a vector database, a query, the context?

18
00:01:05,883 --> 00:01:07,739
这期视频四个都会回答
This video answers all four.

19
00:01:07,983 --> 00:01:10,266
把 README 打开，放在视频旁边
Open the README beside this video.

20
00:01:10,586 --> 00:01:16,452
左上角的进度条显示当前步骤；右上角的灰色标签指向课件
Top left, the tracker shows its step; top right, the gray tag points to the lecture slides.

21
00:01:16,772 --> 00:01:20,823
看到黄色的 your turn 标签，就暂停，自己跑一遍命令
When the yellow your-turn tag appears, pause and run the command;

22
00:01:20,823 --> 00:01:23,066
额外的命令 README 里没有
extra commands aren't in the README.

23
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:27,412
我们录制时没有 Google 的密钥
We recorded without a Google key.

24
00:01:27,732 --> 00:01:30,835
Docker、分块和数据库都是真实运行的
Docker, chunking and the database ran for real;

25
00:01:30,835 --> 00:01:34,004
embedding 用的是课程团队留下的向量
the embeddings are the staff's recorded vectors.

26
00:01:34,324 --> 00:01:35,894
凡是代码调用 Google 的地方
Where the code calls Google,

27
00:01:35,894 --> 00:01:39,145
你会看到命令、真实的报错，以及该看什么
you see the command, the real error, and what to look for.

28
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:42,060
用四个方框讲清 RAG
Here's RAG in four boxes.

29
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:47,927
用户的问题先到 RAG 代码，代码去向量数据库里要相关的文本
The user's question goes to the RAG code, which asks a vector database for related texts.

30
00:01:48,247 --> 00:01:51,676
代码把问题和这些文本拼成一个完整的 prompt
The code joins question and texts into one full prompt,

31
00:01:51,676 --> 00:01:53,858
模型的回答再送回去
and the model's response goes back.

32
00:01:54,178 --> 00:01:56,588
数据库从不和模型直接对话
The database never talks to the model.

33
00:01:56,833 --> 00:01:59,329
打开 RAG 这个方框，里面是两条通道
Open the RAG box and you get two lanes.

34
00:01:59,649 --> 00:02:01,819
上面，先把书切成 chunk
On top, books are cut into chunks,

35
00:02:01,819 --> 00:02:07,436
embedding 模型把每个 chunk 变成一个向量，向量再存进数据库
an embedding model turns each chunk into a vector, and the vectors go into the database.

36
00:02:07,756 --> 00:02:13,366
下面，问题经过同一个模型，只有它的向量会到达数据库
Below, the question goes through the same model, and only its vector reaches the database.

37
00:02:13,616 --> 00:02:17,285
这就是课上那页讲 pipeline 的课件，分三个阶段
This is the pipeline slide from lecture, with three phases.

38
00:02:17,605 --> 00:02:19,717
索引阶段就是上面整条通道
Indexing is the whole top lane.

39
00:02:20,037 --> 00:02:25,755
检索阶段把上下文带进 prompt，模型负责增强和生成
Retrieval brings the context to the prompt, and the model does augmentation and generation.

40
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,755
README 把两条通道叫作 Step 1 和 Step 2
The README calls the two lanes step 1 and step 2,

41
00:02:29,755 --> 00:02:32,667
并给每个方框配了 cli.py 的一个参数
and gives each box one flag of cli.py:

42
00:02:32,667 --> 00:02:35,349
上面是 --chunk、--embed 和 --load
--chunk, --embed and --load on top,

43
00:02:35,349 --> 00:02:37,264
下面是 --query 和 --chat
--query and --chat below.

44
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:38,773
两条规则
Two rules.

45
00:02:38,823 --> 00:02:41,788
上面的通道只跑一次，离线跑，而且很慢
The top lane runs once, offline, and it's slow.

46
00:02:42,108 --> 00:02:44,540
下面的通道每个问题都要跑一次
The bottom lane runs for every question.

47
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:47,862
而且两条通道必须用同一个 embedding 模型
And both lanes must use the same embedding model,

48
00:02:47,862 --> 00:02:51,537
不然问题和这些 chunk 就不在同一个空间里
or the question and the chunks don't live in the same space.

49
00:02:51,783 --> 00:02:53,383
每个方框在哪儿运行？
Where does each box run?

50
00:02:53,554 --> 00:02:55,964
分块器在你自己的 container 里运行
The chunker runs in your own container.

51
00:02:56,284 --> 00:02:57,884
两个模型都在 Google 那边运行
Both models run at Google:

52
00:02:57,884 --> 00:03:02,322
你用自己的密钥，按发送的文本付费，那边没有任何东西一直开着
you pay for the text you send, with your key, and nothing keeps running there.

53
00:03:02,642 --> 00:03:07,164
数据库在第二个 container 里运行，文件放在你的笔记本上
The database runs in a second container, with its files on your laptop.

54
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:10,588
每一步都是一条 python cli.py 命令
Every step is one python cli.py command,

55
00:03:10,588 --> 00:03:12,819
在第一个 container 里运行
inside that first container.

56
00:03:13,139 --> 00:03:15,080
所以，先把它跑起来
So first, let's get it running.

57
00:03:15,317 --> 00:03:17,450
先看 Prerequisites 一节：Docker
Prerequisites first: Docker.

58
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:20,100
这个额外检查会打印它的版本号
This extra check prints its versions;

59
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,997
脚本要的是中间带空格的 docker compose
the script needs docker compose, with a space.

60
00:03:23,317 --> 00:03:26,085
在 Mac 上，提示符看起来不一样
On a Mac your prompt looks different;

61
00:03:26,085 --> 00:03:28,480
在 Windows 上，用 WSL 或 Git Bash
on Windows, use WSL or Git Bash.

62
00:03:28,717 --> 00:03:33,304
README 给了 repo 的链接，但没写 clone 命令，所以命令在这里
The README links the repo but doesn't print the clone command, so here it is.

63
00:03:33,624 --> 00:03:37,880
然后额外做一件事：在 clone 旁边建一个 secrets 目录
Then, as an extra, make a secrets folder beside the clone,

64
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:40,962
并且让 clone 的名字一字不差地叫 llm-rag
and keep the clone's name exactly llm-rag.

65
00:03:41,282 --> 00:03:43,629
暂停一下，在你的课程目录里把两件事都做了
Pause and do both, in your course folder.

66
00:03:45,867 --> 00:03:49,110
接下来是服务账号，在 Google Cloud 控制台里
Now the service account, in the Google Cloud console.

67
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:52,274
建一个叫 llm-service-account 的账号
Create one called llm-service-account,

68
00:03:52,274 --> 00:03:55,118
授予它两个角色：Storage Admin
and grant it two roles: Storage Admin,

69
00:03:55,118 --> 00:03:58,262
还有 Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform User
and Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform User.

70
00:03:58,582 --> 00:04:01,508
打开它的 KEYS 标签页，添加一个 JSON 密钥
Open its keys tab, add a JSON key,

71
00:04:01,508 --> 00:04:05,899
存进 secrets 目录，命名为 llm-service-account.json
and save it in secrets as llm-service-account.json.

72
00:04:06,134 --> 00:04:08,623
这个密钥花的是你项目的钱
That key spends your project's money;

73
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:11,313
.gitignore 文件里没有 secrets 这一行
the .gitignore file has no secrets line,

74
00:04:11,313 --> 00:04:13,601
所以它只有放在 repo 旁边才安全
so it's safe only beside the repo.

75
00:04:13,921 --> 00:04:16,522
还记得第 4 讲的三道关卡吗
Remember the three gates from lecture 4:

76
00:04:16,522 --> 00:04:21,984
密钥说明你是谁，角色说明你能做什么，API 还必须打开
the key says who you are, the role what you may do, and the API must be switched on.

77
00:04:22,234 --> 00:04:23,741
两个小疏漏
Two small slips.

78
00:04:23,791 --> 00:04:25,857
这里没有任何东西用到 Cloud Storage
Nothing here uses Cloud Storage,

79
00:04:25,857 --> 00:04:28,634
所以真正要紧的是 Agent Platform 这个角色
so the Agent Platform role is what matters.

80
00:04:28,954 --> 00:04:33,135
而且 README 一直没说要启用 Vertex AI API
And the README never says to enable the Vertex AI API;

81
00:04:33,135 --> 00:04:36,387
没有它，第一次 embedding 调用就会失败
without it, the first embedding call fails

82
00:04:36,387 --> 00:04:39,407
重试 5 次后报 service disabled
with SERVICE_DISABLED, after 5 retries.

83
00:04:39,727 --> 00:04:43,780
现在就暂停，全部弄好：账号、角色、密钥和 API
Pause and do it all now: account, roles, key, and API.

84
00:04:46,017 --> 00:04:49,452
下一节的第 1 步：cd llm-rag
Step 1 of the next section: cd llm-rag.

85
00:04:49,772 --> 00:04:54,102
额外看一眼，能看到这些脚本、compose 文件、cli.py
An extra look shows the scripts, the compose file, cli.py,

86
00:04:54,102 --> 00:04:57,238
以及这期视频录制时用的 commit
and the commit this video was recorded on.

87
00:04:57,484 --> 00:04:59,372
第 2 步在编辑器里做
Step 2: in your editor,

88
00:04:59,372 --> 00:05:03,396
把第 7 行的 GCP project 变量改成自己的项目 ID
set GCP_PROJECT on line 7 to your own Project ID,

89
00:05:03,396 --> 00:05:05,121
是 ID，不是项目名称
the ID, not the name.

90
00:05:05,441 --> 00:05:07,041
第 8 行别动
Leave line 8 alone.

91
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:10,732
跳过这一步，你的调用就会发到课程的项目上，然后失败
Skip this, and your calls go to the course's project and fail.

92
00:05:11,052 --> 00:05:12,652
暂停一下，改好它
Pause and edit.

93
00:05:15,567 --> 00:05:18,480
第 4 讲把两个 container 放在一个网络上
Lecture 4 put two containers on one network;

94
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:21,327
第 3 讲通过挂载把密钥带了进来
lecture 3 brought a key in through a mount.

95
00:05:21,647 --> 00:05:24,058
今天：两件事一起做，只用一条命令
Today: both at once, with one command.

96
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:27,686
这个脚本 docker-shell.sh 导出三个值
The script, docker-shell.sh, exports three values:

97
00:05:27,686 --> 00:05:32,428
你的项目、密钥在 container 里的路径，还有 image 名
your project, the key's path inside the container, and the image name.

98
00:05:32,748 --> 00:05:37,740
然后它调用 docker compose run，加上 --rm，只跑那一个服务
Then it calls docker compose run, with --rm, for that one service.

99
00:05:37,984 --> 00:05:40,723
这个 compose 文件把整张图都画出来了
The compose file draws the whole picture:

100
00:05:40,723 --> 00:05:43,929
一个网络，按名字指定，上面是 CLI 服务
one network, by name, and the CLI service on it,

101
00:05:43,929 --> 00:05:47,136
image 没有的话就用这个目录构建
with an image built from this folder if missing.

102
00:05:47,384 --> 00:05:51,736
两个挂载把这个 repo 放到 /app，把 secrets 放到 /secrets
Two mounts put the repo onto /app and secrets onto /secrets.

103
00:05:52,056 --> 00:05:56,130
两个空位接收脚本给的值，这个服务还依赖 Chroma
Two slots take the script's values, and the service depends on Chroma.

104
00:05:56,367 --> 00:05:59,696
Chroma 服务运行的是来自 Docker Hub 的数据库
The Chroma service runs the database from Docker Hub,

105
00:05:59,696 --> 00:06:01,160
用一个固定的名字
under a fixed name.

106
00:06:01,210 --> 00:06:03,730
它把 port 8000 发布到你的笔记本上
It publishes port 8000 to your laptop,

107
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:09,103
把数据放在 docker-volumes 目录里，还让课程的网页工具连进来
keeps its data in the docker-volumes/ folder, and lets the course's web tools in.

108
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:13,983
再看 Dockerfile：虚拟环境在 /.venv
From the Dockerfile: the virtual environment lives in /.venv,

109
00:06:13,983 --> 00:06:17,478
在 /app 外面，所以代码的挂载盖不住它
outside /app, so the code mount can't hide it.

110
00:06:17,798 --> 00:06:21,852
在笔记本上改 cli.py，再跑一次就行；不用重新构建
Edit cli.py on your laptop and rerun; no rebuild.

111
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:24,895
第 3 步：sh docker-shell.sh
Step 3: sh docker-shell.sh.

112
00:06:25,215 --> 00:06:27,087
Compose 会 pull Chroma 的 image
Compose pulls Chroma's image,

113
00:06:27,087 --> 00:06:30,890
建好网络，并且先建 Chroma 的 container
creates the network, and creates the Chroma container first.

114
00:06:31,134 --> 00:06:33,865
然后是这个：看起来像报错，其实不是
Then this, which looks like an error but isn't.

115
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:39,792
Compose 在 Docker Hub 上没找到叫 llm-rag-cli 的 image
Compose first asks Docker Hub for an image called llm-rag-cli, finds none,

116
00:06:39,792 --> 00:06:41,459
就改为自己构建
and builds it instead.

117
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,705
这里构建用了 81 秒
The build took 81 seconds here.

118
00:06:44,025 --> 00:06:46,863
构建上下文有 112 MB
Its context was 112 megabytes.

119
00:06:47,183 --> 00:06:52,175
其中大部分是 git 历史，里面还留着课程团队数据库的旧拷贝
Most of it is git history, which still holds an old copy of the staff's database.

120
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:55,588
因为没有 .dockerignore 文件，image 会把它留下来
With no .dockerignore file, the image keeps it.

121
00:06:55,834 --> 00:07:03,535
然后是横幅：Python 3.12.15 和 uv 0.13.1，都是录制时的版本
Then the banner: Python 3.12.15 and uv 0.13.1, at the time of recording.

122
00:07:03,855 --> 00:07:07,204
它在激活之前就说已经激活了：只是显示问题
It says activated before it activates: cosmetic.

123
00:07:07,450 --> 00:07:09,233
你现在到了 container 的提示符
You're at the container's prompt.

124
00:07:09,498 --> 00:07:14,426
提示符里 @ 符号后面是 container ID；每次运行都会变
The part after the at sign is the container's ID; it changes every run.

125
00:07:14,746 --> 00:07:16,496
暂停一下，走到这个提示符
Pause, and get to this prompt.

126
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:22,137
用额外检查核对这张图
Check the picture with extras:

127
00:07:22,137 --> 00:07:25,977
在笔记本上开第二个终端，cd 进 llm-rag
open a second laptop terminal and cd into llm-rag.

128
00:07:26,297 --> 00:07:28,633
用 docker ps 这条命令可以看到 Chroma
The docker ps command shows Chroma

129
00:07:28,633 --> 00:07:30,350
port 8000 已经发布出去了
with port 8000 published.

130
00:07:30,670 --> 00:07:34,473
但 CLI container 并不叫 llm-rag-cli
But the CLI container isn't called llm-rag-cli:

131
00:07:34,473 --> 00:07:36,900
compose run 会忽略这个名字
compose run ignores that name.

132
00:07:37,133 --> 00:07:38,533
再用 docker inspect
And docker inspect,

133
00:07:38,533 --> 00:07:41,272
带上 docker ps 给出的名字，就能列出挂载
with the name from docker ps, lists the mounts.

134
00:07:41,592 --> 00:07:44,848
这个 repo 在 /app，secrets 在 /secrets
The repo is on /app, secrets on /secrets,

135
00:07:44,848 --> 00:07:48,738
docker-volumes 目录在 Chroma 的 /data
and the docker-volumes/ folder on Chroma's /data.

136
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:53,324
在 container 里，你的项目 ID 和密钥的路径都传进来了
Inside the container, your Project ID and the key's path arrived.

137
00:07:53,644 --> 00:07:56,651
我们的 secrets 目录是空的，没有密钥
Our secrets folder is empty, with no key;

138
00:07:56,651 --> 00:07:58,998
你的应该能列出那个 JSON 文件
yours should list the JSON file.

139
00:07:59,233 --> 00:08:03,009
CLI 通过网络的电话簿，按名字找到 Chroma
The CLI finds Chroma by name, through the network's phone book.

140
00:08:03,329 --> 00:08:07,357
在你的笔记本上，心跳通过 localhost:8000 回来
From your laptop, the heartbeat comes through localhost:8000,

141
00:08:07,357 --> 00:08:10,262
这就是发布出去的那扇门，给你和你的浏览器用
the published door for you and your browser.

142
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:14,301
Docker 已经在你的笔记本上建好了 Chroma 的数据目录
Docker already created Chroma's data folder on your laptop,

143
00:08:14,301 --> 00:08:17,135
属主是 root，数据库文件就在里面
owned by root, with the database file in it.

144
00:08:17,455 --> 00:08:20,270
在 Linux 上，以后删它要用 sudo
On Linux, deleting it later will need sudo.

145
00:08:20,516 --> 00:08:22,564
接下来是两个陷阱，我们故意踩一下
Now two traps, hit on purpose.

146
00:08:22,884 --> 00:08:25,700
陷阱一：自己敲 compose 命令
Trap one: typing the compose command yourself.

147
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:30,715
两个变量都是空的，连分块都在启动时就挂了
Both variables come out blank, and even chunking dies at startup,

148
00:08:30,715 --> 00:08:33,532
cli.py 在那里创建 Google 客户端
where cli.py creates its Google client,

149
00:08:33,532 --> 00:08:36,132
去找一个没有名字的密钥文件
looking for a key file with no name.

150
00:08:36,452 --> 00:08:38,202
一定要通过脚本启动
Always start through the script.

151
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:40,644
陷阱二：clone 用了别的名字
Trap two: a clone with another name,

152
00:08:40,644 --> 00:08:43,143
比如下载 zip 包解压出来的那种目录
like the folder a zip download gives you.

153
00:08:43,463 --> 00:08:46,720
这个 compose 文件挂载的是名叫 llm-rag 的目录
The compose file mounts a folder named llm-rag,

154
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:51,015
所以 Docker 会建一个空目录，属主是 root，盖在你的代码上
so Docker creates an empty one, owned by root, over your code.

155
00:08:51,335 --> 00:08:53,916
名字保持不变，再把多出来的那个目录删掉
Keep the name, and delete the stray folder.

156
00:08:54,166 --> 00:09:00,047
最后一个怪现象：image 的 tag 叫 latest，而三个版本号对不上
One last oddity: the image tag called latest, and three version numbers that don't match;

157
00:09:00,047 --> 00:09:01,647
团队应该 pin 一个固定的 tag
a team should pin a tag.

158
00:09:01,953 --> 00:09:06,241
暂停一下，试试这些检查；最要紧的是你放在 /secrets 里的密钥
Pause and try these checks; your key in /secrets matters most.

159
00:09:09,583 --> 00:09:11,354
建索引从分块开始
Indexing starts with chunking.

160
00:09:11,674 --> 00:09:14,689
一整本书只用一个向量，会把书里的话题平均掉
One vector for a whole book averages its topics,

161
00:09:14,689 --> 00:09:17,263
于是每个问题都会取回整本书
so every question fetches the whole book.

162
00:09:17,583 --> 00:09:21,935
每次都发 11 本书，又慢又贵，得到的还是垃圾
Sending 11 books each time is slow, costly, and gives garbage.

163
00:09:22,255 --> 00:09:25,028
一个 chunk 小到可以被找到，也小到可以贴进去
A chunk is small enough to find, and to paste.

164
00:09:26,866 --> 00:09:30,173
第 1 步是一个链接：README 里的 chunk 可视化工具
Step 1 is a link: the README's chunk visualizer.

165
00:09:30,493 --> 00:09:34,824
在 Chrome 里打开，拖拖滑块；它展示的想法是这样的
Open it in Chrome and play with the sliders; here's the idea it shows.

166
00:09:35,666 --> 00:09:37,565
按字符切分就是一把尺子
Character splitting is a ruler.

167
00:09:37,885 --> 00:09:43,688
第 185 和 186 行设定了 350 个字符的窗口
Lines 185 and 186 set windows of 350 characters,

168
00:09:43,688 --> 00:09:45,863
相邻窗口重叠 20 个
overlapping by 20.

169
00:09:46,183 --> 00:09:52,626
分隔符是空的，所以它数的是字符，不是单词，每次前进 330 个
The separator is empty, so it counts characters, not words, stepping 330 at a time.

170
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:57,157
授课老师的故事长 7808 个字符
The instructor's story is 7,808 characters long.

171
00:09:57,477 --> 00:10:02,085
窗口大小 350，重叠 20：会切出多少个 chunk？
Windows of 350 that overlap by 20: how many chunks?

172
00:10:10,933 --> 00:10:17,290
第一个窗口取 350 个字符，之后每个窗口新增 330 个
The first window takes 350 characters, and each one after it adds 330 new ones.

173
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:23,968
剩下的 7458 个字符还要 23 个窗口：一共 24 个 chunk
7,458 more characters need 23 more windows: 24 chunks.

174
00:10:25,033 --> 00:10:30,302
第 2 步：python cli.py --chunk，用 char-split
Step 2: python cli.py --chunk --chunk_type char-split.

175
00:10:30,622 --> 00:10:35,572
它读入 11 本书，打印每本书的 chunk 数；故事得到 24 个
It reads 11 books and prints each book's chunk count; the story gets 24.

176
00:10:35,892 --> 00:10:38,900
不需要密钥：代码里的这个分支从不调用 Google
No key needed: this branch never calls Google.

177
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,820
暂停一下，自己跑一遍
Pause and run it.

178
00:10:42,616 --> 00:10:49,891
额外数一下 chunk 文件的行数：故事是 24 行，一共 8248 行
An extra line count of the chunk files: 24 for the story, and 8,248 in total.

179
00:10:50,133 --> 00:10:51,754
额外看一眼接缝
An extra look at the seam.

180
00:10:52,074 --> 00:10:55,189
第 0 个 chunk 停在 accomplish 这个词的前两个字母上
Chunk 0 stops two letters into the word accomplish.

181
00:10:55,509 --> 00:10:57,515
第 1 个 chunk 往回退 20 个字符
Chunk 1 backs up 20 characters,

182
00:10:57,515 --> 00:11:01,333
退到 things 的最后一个字母，所以 accomplish 又完整了
to the last letter of things, so accomplish is whole again.

183
00:11:01,653 --> 00:11:04,896
课上的例子里，切出的块首尾相接，没有重叠
The lecture's pieces sit end to end, with no overlap.

184
00:11:05,133 --> 00:11:07,326
这些 chunk 文件落在 outputs 目录里
The chunk files land in outputs/,

185
00:11:07,326 --> 00:11:09,784
就在你的笔记本上，git 会忽略它们
on your laptop, and git ignores them.

186
00:11:10,104 --> 00:11:11,815
一本 Gutenberg 书的第 0 行
Row 0 of a Gutenberg book

187
00:11:11,815 --> 00:11:16,193
是 Project Gutenberg 的开头声明：这些书开头是声明
is the Project Gutenberg header: these books start with a header

188
00:11:16,193 --> 00:11:19,682
结尾是许可证，两者都和正文一样切成了 chunk
and end with a license, both chunked like the rest.

189
00:11:21,617 --> 00:11:26,289
递归切分只给了 chunk 大小，还是 350
Recursive splitting gets only a chunk size, the same 350.

190
00:11:26,609 --> 00:11:28,209
没有指定重叠
No overlap is given.

191
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,667
它就像一把会找最佳缝隙的剪刀
It works like scissors that look for the best gap.

192
00:11:31,987 --> 00:11:35,717
先找段落之间的空行，再找换行
First a blank line between paragraphs, then a line break,

193
00:11:35,717 --> 00:11:39,645
再找空格，实在不行才切在单个字符上
then a space, and only as a last resort, a single character.

194
00:11:39,965 --> 00:11:42,014
所以每个切点都落在单词之间
So every cut falls between words.

195
00:11:42,650 --> 00:11:46,298
第 3 步：同一条命令，chunk type 换成 recursive-split
Step 3: the same command with --chunk_type recursive-split.

196
00:11:46,618 --> 00:11:53,893
故事现在切出 35 个 chunk，额外数一下行数，一共 14228 个
The story now makes 35 chunks, and an extra line count gives 14,228 in total.

197
00:11:54,213 --> 00:11:55,813
暂停一下，自己跑一遍
Pause and run it.

198
00:11:57,600 --> 00:12:00,203
同样的 chunk 大小，350
Same chunk size, 350.

199
00:12:00,523 --> 00:12:06,560
那为什么是 14228 个 chunk，而不是 8248 个？
So why 14,228 chunks instead of 8,248?

200
00:12:18,350 --> 00:12:19,950
看看前几个 chunk
Look at the first chunks.

201
00:12:20,142 --> 00:12:22,586
第 1 个 chunk 又从 Chapter One 开始
Chunk 1 starts again with Chapter One,

202
00:12:22,586 --> 00:12:24,451
重复了第 0 个 chunk 的结尾
repeating the end of chunk 0.

203
00:12:24,771 --> 00:12:26,792
这个切分器的库默认
The splitter's library default

204
00:12:26,792 --> 00:12:31,577
最多重叠 200 个字符，README 从没提过
is an overlap of up to 200 characters, which the README never mentions.

205
00:12:31,897 --> 00:12:34,542
在边界处切开，也会让 chunk 变短
Cutting at boundaries also makes chunks shorter.

206
00:12:34,784 --> 00:12:38,155
重叠是一份保险，防止把一个意思切成两半
Overlap is insurance against cutting an idea in half.

207
00:12:38,475 --> 00:12:42,272
但每个重复的字符都要向量化、存储，还要付钱
But every repeated character is embedded, stored, and paid for.

208
00:12:42,592 --> 00:12:45,941
想要别的值，就自己设置 chunk overlap 参数
If you want a different value, set chunk_overlap yourself.

209
00:12:46,184 --> 00:12:50,685
课上的观点是：理想的 chunk 应该顺着文档自身的结构
The lecture's point is that ideal chunks follow the document's own structure.

210
00:12:51,005 --> 00:12:54,440
递归切分做到了一部分，靠的是段落
Recursive splitting goes part of the way, using paragraphs.

211
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:57,554
第二部分的语义分块走得更远
Semantic chunking, in part 2, goes further.

212
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,164
接下来是 embedding 模型
Next, the embedding model.

213
00:13:01,484 --> 00:13:05,256
它把每个 chunk 变成一个向量，也就是一串数字
It turns each chunk into one vector, a list of numbers,

214
00:13:05,256 --> 00:13:08,549
让意思相近的指向相近的方向
so similar meanings point in similar directions:

215
00:13:08,549 --> 00:13:12,321
在这张示意图里，讲凝乳的挨着讲凝乳的，许可证文本在别处
in this sketch, curd near curd, license text elsewhere.

216
00:13:12,867 --> 00:13:16,216
课上的性格游戏把这件事讲得很具体
The personality game from lecture makes this concrete:

217
00:13:16,216 --> 00:13:19,566
三个候选人中哪个最像授课老师？
which of three candidates is most like the instructor?

218
00:13:19,886 --> 00:13:23,171
五个分数把每个人变成一个五维向量
Five scores make each person a five-number vector.

219
00:13:23,491 --> 00:13:28,205
余弦相似度只比较夹角，选中的是第一个候选人
Cosine similarity compares only the angle, and picks the first candidate.

220
00:13:28,450 --> 00:13:34,146
点积还会算上长度，会选中第二个候选人，也就是箭头更长的那个
The dot product also counts length, and would pick the second candidate, whose arrow is longer.

221
00:13:34,466 --> 00:13:38,647
所以度量是一个选择；对文本来说，常用的是余弦
So a measure is a choice; for text, cosine is the usual one.

222
00:13:39,183 --> 00:13:46,543
教程用的模型是 gemini-embedding-001，原生返回 3072 个数
The tutorial's model, gemini-embedding-001, natively returns 3,072 numbers.

223
00:13:46,863 --> 00:13:49,594
代码只要前 256 个
The code asks for the first 256.

224
00:13:49,914 --> 00:13:53,199
模型训练时就让这段前缀单独也能用
The model is trained to make that prefix useful alone.

225
00:13:53,433 --> 00:13:56,441
这些 chunk 每批 100 个发给模型
Chunks go to the model in batches of 100.

226
00:13:56,761 --> 00:13:59,915
遇到 API 错误，它最多重试 5 次
On an API error, it retries up to 5 times,

227
00:13:59,915 --> 00:14:02,393
等待时间从 5 秒开始逐次翻倍
doubling the wait from 5 seconds.

228
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:05,513
你的问题之后也会用这同一个模型
Your question will use this same model, later.

229
00:14:05,833 --> 00:14:08,521
现在是 chunk，之后是问题：同一个模型
Chunks now, questions later: one model.

230
00:14:08,767 --> 00:14:14,143
第 1 步：python cli.py --embed，用 char-split
Step 1: python cli.py --embed --chunk_type char-split.

231
00:14:14,463 --> 00:14:16,191
这是首次调用 Google
It's the first call to Google.

232
00:14:16,511 --> 00:14:20,906
在我们的机器上，它读入第一本书，然后停住了：没有密钥文件
On our machine it reads the first book, then stops at the missing key file.

233
00:14:21,226 --> 00:14:22,826
在你的机器上，它能跑通
On yours, it runs.

234
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,537
有密钥的话，要找的是每本书的文件
With your key, look for each book's file,

235
00:14:25,537 --> 00:14:28,817
5 秒的停顿、一张带 embedding 列的表
a 5-second pause, a table with an embedding column,

236
00:14:28,817 --> 00:14:31,583
以及 chunk 旁边新出现的 embeddings 文件
and new embeddings files beside the chunks.

237
00:14:31,817 --> 00:14:34,974
如果你那边失败了，或者一直在重试，就去读报错
If yours fails, or keeps retrying, read the error.

238
00:14:35,294 --> 00:14:38,430
找不到密钥文件：检查 secrets 目录里它的名字
Key file not found: check its name in secrets.

239
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:40,250
报 permission denied
PERMISSION_DENIED:

240
00:14:40,250 --> 00:14:44,617
改好项目 ID 或角色，然后退出，重新运行脚本
fix the Project ID or the role, then exit and start the script again.

241
00:14:44,937 --> 00:14:47,817
报 service disabled：把 API 打开
SERVICE_DISABLED: switch on the API.

242
00:14:48,067 --> 00:14:50,755
第 2 步对 recursive-split 做同样的事
Step 2 does the same for recursive-split.

243
00:14:51,075 --> 00:14:53,917
暂停一下，用你的密钥两条都跑一遍
Pause and run both, with your key:

244
00:14:53,917 --> 00:14:58,264
大约 89 次和 148 次调用，按我们的估算只要几美分
about 89 and 148 calls, a few cents by our estimate.

245
00:14:58,584 --> 00:15:00,184
具体以现行的价目表为准
Check the current price list.

246
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:05,325
视频接下来用课程团队自己的输出
The video goes on with the staff's own outputs,

247
00:15:05,325 --> 00:15:08,437
它们曾经 commit 过，至今还在每个 clone 的历史里
once committed and still in every clone's history.

248
00:15:08,757 --> 00:15:11,259
他们的 chunk 文件和我们的逐字节相同
Their chunk files match ours byte for byte,

249
00:15:11,259 --> 00:15:13,877
所以他们的向量就是这条命令会生成的向量
so their vectors are what this command makes.

250
00:15:14,117 --> 00:15:16,442
额外检查一下故事的向量
An extra check on the story's vectors.

251
00:15:16,762 --> 00:15:19,898
24 行，每行 256 个数
24 rows of 256 numbers.

252
00:15:20,218 --> 00:15:26,106
它们的长度在 0.369 到 0.402 之间，不是 1
Their lengths run from 0.369 to 0.402, not 1.

253
00:15:26,350 --> 00:15:29,741
等我们加载这些向量时，数据库会按余弦来比较
When we load them, the database will compare by cosine,

254
00:15:29,741 --> 00:15:31,961
而这些箭头的长度都不到 1
and these arrows are shorter than 1.

255
00:15:32,281 --> 00:15:34,649
这会改变哪些 chunk 算是最近的吗？
Does that change which chunks count as nearest?

256
00:15:43,483 --> 00:15:45,851
不会：余弦只看夹角
No: cosine only sees the angle.

257
00:15:46,171 --> 00:15:49,007
要是用直线距离，也就是 Chroma 的默认值
With straight-line distance, Chroma's default,

258
00:15:49,007 --> 00:15:53,446
或者用点积，长度就会渗进排名：这就是那个游戏的教训
or a dot product, length would leak into the ranking: the game's lesson.

259
00:15:56,283 --> 00:15:59,455
普通数据库回答的是精确的问题
An ordinary database answers precise questions,

260
00:15:59,455 --> 00:16:05,392
比如价格在 10 到 50 之间，但它找不到意思和问题相近的行
like a price between 10 and 50, but it can't find rows whose meaning is like a question.

261
00:16:05,712 --> 00:16:07,312
向量数据库可以
A vector database can.

262
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:09,385
每个 chunk 变成一条记录
Each chunk becomes a record:

263
00:16:09,385 --> 00:16:13,907
一个 ID，文本，包含书名、作者和年份的元数据，还有向量
an ID, the text, metadata with book, author and year, and the vector.

264
00:16:14,227 --> 00:16:18,131
这个 ID 是对书名加行号做哈希得到的，所以是稳定的
The ID hashes the book's name plus the row number, so it's stable.

265
00:16:18,366 --> 00:16:21,459
记录放进一个 collection，每种 chunk type 一个
Records go into a collection, one per chunk type.

266
00:16:21,779 --> 00:16:24,847
而 load 这一步先删掉它，再重新创建
The load step deletes it and creates it again,

267
00:16:24,847 --> 00:16:28,649
用余弦作为度量：每次 load 都是完全重建
with cosine as its measure: every load is a full rebuild.

268
00:16:28,883 --> 00:16:32,168
拿问题和每个向量逐一比较，数据量一大就很慢
Comparing a question with every vector is slow at scale.

269
00:16:32,488 --> 00:16:36,502
所以数据库会建一个索引，就是这几页课件说的那种
So the database builds an index, in these slides' sense:

270
00:16:36,502 --> 00:16:41,448
一张叫 HNSW 的分层图，搜索几步就能一层层跳下来
a layered graph called HNSW, where a search hops down in a few steps.

271
00:16:41,683 --> 00:16:46,931
第 1 步：python cli.py --load，chunk type 用 char-split
Step 1: python cli.py --load --chunk_type char-split.

272
00:16:47,251 --> 00:16:50,291
我们第一次运行时还没有 embedding
On our first run there were no embeddings yet:

273
00:16:50,291 --> 00:16:53,331
它建了一个空的 collection，找到 0 个文件
it made an empty collection and found 0 files.

274
00:16:53,651 --> 00:16:56,510
如果你看到 0，说明你的 embed 那一步没跑完
If you see 0, your embed step didn't finish.

275
00:16:56,750 --> 00:17:01,943
用课程团队留下的向量，同一条命令会删掉那个空的 collection
On the staff's recorded vectors, the same command deletes that empty collection

276
00:17:01,943 --> 00:17:04,835
读入 11 个带 embedding 列的文件
and reads 11 files with an embedding column.

277
00:17:05,155 --> 00:17:10,318
它插入 8248 条记录，每批 500 条
It inserts 8,248 records, in batches of 500.

278
00:17:10,566 --> 00:17:15,707
第 2 步加载 recursive-split，14228 条记录
Step 2 loads recursive-split, 14,228 records.

279
00:17:16,027 --> 00:17:17,734
暂停一下，两次 load 都跑一遍
Pause and run both loads.

280
00:17:19,983 --> 00:17:21,213
额外检查一下
An extra check:

281
00:17:21,213 --> 00:17:26,703
两个 collection 现在的维度都是 256，由第一次插入决定
both collections now have dimension 256, fixed by the first insert.

282
00:17:26,950 --> 00:17:29,244
还有一本书没有作者和年份
And one book has no author or year:

283
00:17:29,244 --> 00:17:32,454
一个小疏漏，代码在第一个点就把文件名截断了
a small slip cuts its file name at the first dot.

284
00:17:32,774 --> 00:17:37,697
只去掉扩展名，删掉 outputs 目录里这本书的旧文件
Split off only the extension, delete that book's old files in outputs/,

285
00:17:37,697 --> 00:17:39,984
然后重新分块、向量化、加载
then chunk, embed and load again.

286
00:17:40,233 --> 00:17:43,278
你笔记本上的 docker-volumes 目录里
The docker-volumes/ folder on your laptop

287
00:17:43,278 --> 00:17:47,585
现在有一个 60 MB 的 SQLite 文件，还有两个索引目录
now holds a 60-megabyte SQLite file and two index folders,

288
00:17:47,585 --> 00:17:50,110
每个 collection 一个，属主都是 root
one per collection, owned by root.

289
00:17:50,430 --> 00:17:52,308
README 说它是持久化的
The README calls it persistent.

290
00:17:52,550 --> 00:17:55,622
第 3 步是一个链接，指向课程的 Chroma UI
Step 3 is a link to the course's Chroma UI.

291
00:17:55,942 --> 00:18:00,320
在 Chrome 里打开，它会通过 port 8000 读取你本地的数据库
Opened in Chrome, it reads your local database through port 8000;

292
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:03,216
Chroma 的设置放行了课程的网站
Chroma's settings let the course's site in.

293
00:18:03,466 --> 00:18:06,090
上面这条通道完成了：索引建好了
The top lane is done: the index is built.

294
00:18:06,410 --> 00:18:08,565
第二部分，我们来向它提问
In part 2, we ask it questions.

295
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:13,463
第一部分，我们建好了索引：分块、向量化、加载
In part 1, we built the index: chunk, embed, load.

296
00:18:13,783 --> 00:18:15,383
第二部分让它派上用场
Part 2 puts it to work.

297
00:18:15,703 --> 00:18:19,585
不过先测试一下：合上笔记本，索引还在吗？
But first, a test: does the index survive closing the laptop?

298
00:18:19,833 --> 00:18:21,646
怎么离开，README 里没写
Leaving isn't in the README.

299
00:18:21,966 --> 00:18:27,065
输入 exit，再在笔记本上列出所有 container：docker ps -a
Type exit, and on the laptop, list every container with docker ps -a.

300
00:18:27,385 --> 00:18:30,720
CLI container 已经没了，退出时就被删掉了
The CLI container is gone, removed on exit,

301
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:34,831
但 Chroma 还在运行，port 8000 也还被占着
but Chroma is still up, and port 8000 is still taken.

302
00:18:35,067 --> 00:18:38,736
要停掉它，在 repo 目录里运行：docker compose down
To stop it, run docker compose down from the repo folder.

303
00:18:39,056 --> 00:18:41,510
有两条警告，说这两个变量没有设置
Two warnings say the variables aren't set.

304
00:18:41,830 --> 00:18:44,349
它们无害：只有脚本会设置这两个变量
They're harmless: only the script sets them,

305
00:18:44,349 --> 00:18:46,352
而 down 这条命令两个都不需要
and the down command needs neither.

306
00:18:46,672 --> 00:18:49,019
然后 Chroma 和网络就删掉了
Then Chroma and the network are removed.

307
00:18:49,267 --> 00:18:50,867
现在什么都没在运行了
Nothing is running now.

308
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:53,877
但你磁盘上的 docker-volumes 目录里
But the docker-volumes/ folder on your disk

309
00:18:53,877 --> 00:18:57,324
数据库文件和两个索引目录都还在
still holds the database file and both index folders,

310
00:18:57,324 --> 00:19:00,381
outputs 目录里的 chunk 文件也原封未动
and your chunk files in outputs/ are untouched.

311
00:19:00,617 --> 00:19:04,329
改天回来，再跑一次：sh docker-shell.sh
Back another day: sh docker-shell.sh again.

312
00:19:04,649 --> 00:19:07,209
不 pull，也不构建：image 已经有了
No pull, no build: the image exists.

313
00:19:07,529 --> 00:19:12,036
要是 git pull 改了依赖或 Dockerfile
After a git pull that changes the dependencies or the Dockerfile,

314
00:19:12,036 --> 00:19:14,185
先运行：docker compose build
run docker compose build first.

315
00:19:14,505 --> 00:19:16,105
暂停一下，重新启动
Pause and restart.

316
00:19:19,267 --> 00:19:24,273
两个额外检查：两个 collection 都回来了，维度都是 256
Two extra checks: both collections are back, with dimension 256,

317
00:19:24,273 --> 00:19:29,358
一条叫 --get 的额外命令，返回的还是那 10 条记录的 ID
and an extra command called --get returns the same 10 record IDs.

318
00:19:29,678 --> 00:19:33,133
那个 container 是一次性的；数据从来不住在它里面
The container was disposable; the data never lived in it.

319
00:19:34,483 --> 00:19:36,083
现在看下面那条通道
Now the bottom lane.

320
00:19:36,211 --> 00:19:39,344
问题经过同一个 embedding 模型
The question goes through the same embedding model

321
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:43,102
变成一个查询向量，和那些 chunk 在同一个空间里
and becomes a query vector, in the same space as the chunks.

322
00:19:43,422 --> 00:19:45,896
查询就是找它的最近邻
Querying means finding its nearest neighbors.

323
00:19:46,133 --> 00:19:49,290
课上拿查询给每个存好的向量打分
The lecture scores every stored vector against the query.

324
00:19:49,610 --> 00:19:56,160
0.57、0.77、0.43、0.93
0.57, 0.77, 0.43, 0.93.

325
00:19:56,480 --> 00:20:00,362
按分数排序，保留 top K，K 是事先定好的
Sort by score, and keep the top K, with K fixed in advance.

326
00:20:00,682 --> 00:20:02,282
这份代码用的是 10
This code uses 10.

327
00:20:02,350 --> 00:20:06,766
有一点不同：课上按相似度排名，越高越好
One difference: the lecture ranks by similarity, where higher is better.

328
00:20:07,086 --> 00:20:12,569
Chroma 报的是余弦距离，也就是 1 减去相似度，越小越近
Chroma reports cosine distance, one minus the similarity, where smaller is closer.

329
00:20:12,889 --> 00:20:15,022
顺序一样，方向相反
Same order, opposite direction.

330
00:20:15,266 --> 00:20:17,320
而且一次查询总会返回 K 个结果
And a query returns K results

331
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:20,791
只要有 K 个 chunk 可用，不管相关不相关
whenever K chunks are available, relevant or not.

332
00:20:21,111 --> 00:20:23,864
这份代码里没有任何地方设置距离阈值
Nothing in this code sets a distance threshold.

333
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:27,223
代码里，query 函数先设定问题
In the code, the query function sets the question,

334
00:20:27,223 --> 00:20:30,345
用同一个 Google 模型把它变成向量
turns it into a vector with the same Google model,

335
00:20:30,345 --> 00:20:32,718
再打开这个 chunk type 的 collection
and opens the chunk type's collection.

336
00:20:32,966 --> 00:20:38,278
第 1 步：python cli.py --query，用 char-split
Step 1: python cli.py --query --chunk_type char-split.

337
00:20:38,598 --> 00:20:41,166
先说一个小疏漏：它打印的是 load 这个词
A small slip first: it prints load(),

338
00:20:41,166 --> 00:20:43,526
这个标签是从加载的代码里抄过来的
a label copied from the load code.

339
00:20:43,846 --> 00:20:45,426
然后它连上了 Chroma
Then it connects to Chroma,

340
00:20:45,426 --> 00:20:49,521
但在把问题向量化时卡在了密钥上，还没开始搜索
but stops at the key while embedding the question, before it searches.

341
00:20:49,766 --> 00:20:54,182
问题必须先变成向量，数据库才能拿它来比较
The question must become a vector before the database can compare it,

342
00:20:54,182 --> 00:20:57,958
而只有同一个 Google 模型才能做出同一个空间里的向量
and only the same Google model makes one in the same space.

343
00:20:58,200 --> 00:21:00,632
第 2 步用 recursive-split 再跑一次
Step 2 runs it on recursive-split.

344
00:21:00,952 --> 00:21:06,605
有密钥的话，要找的是：256 个 embedding 值、查询，以及结果
With your key, look for 256 embedding values, the query, and the results.

345
00:21:06,925 --> 00:21:10,522
结果是列表套列表：每个查询一个列表
The results are lists of lists: one list per query,

346
00:21:10,522 --> 00:21:13,837
里面装着 ID、距离、元数据和文档
holding IDs, distances, metadata and documents.

347
00:21:14,157 --> 00:21:15,757
暂停一下，两条都跑一遍
Pause and run both.

348
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:21,156
所以后面 chat 这一步读的是 documents 的第 0 项
That's why chat, later, reads documents[0].

349
00:21:21,476 --> 00:21:25,892
我们没有录到任何结果，所以接下来直接去问加载好的数据库
No results were recorded, so next we ask the loaded database directly.

350
00:21:27,233 --> 00:21:30,881
代码发出的查询是这样的：10 个结果，加两个过滤条件
Here's the query the code sends: 10 results and two filters.

351
00:21:31,201 --> 00:21:35,084
元数据过滤只留一本书：The Complete Book of Cheese
The metadata filter keeps one book, The Complete Book of Cheese.

352
00:21:35,404 --> 00:21:38,689
文档过滤留下包含 Italian 的 chunk
The document filter keeps chunks that contain Italian.

353
00:21:38,933 --> 00:21:40,896
问题问的是 Tolminc
The question is about Tolminc.

354
00:21:41,216 --> 00:21:43,136
那 10 个结果会讲什么？
What will the 10 results be about?

355
00:21:51,983 --> 00:21:55,076
额外检查一下：在加载好的 collection 里数一数
An extra check counts them in the loaded collection.

356
00:21:55,396 --> 00:22:01,754
在 8248 个 chunk 里，按书过滤留下 1355 个
Of 8,248 chunks, the book filter keeps 1,355.

357
00:22:02,074 --> 00:22:04,202
再按 Italian 这个词过滤，留下 64 个
The word Italian keeps 64.

358
00:22:04,420 --> 00:22:06,020
有多少提到 Tolminc？
How many mention Tolminc?

359
00:22:06,319 --> 00:22:08,371
一个都没有。现在来搜索
None. Now a search.

360
00:22:08,691 --> 00:22:11,921
真正的问题要靠 Google 才能变成向量
The real question needs Google to become a vector,

361
00:22:11,921 --> 00:22:15,731
所以我们用一个替身：故事里一个 chunk 存好的向量
so we use a stand-in: the stored vector of one story chunk.

362
00:22:16,051 --> 00:22:20,544
不加过滤，它最近的 10 个全都来自这个故事
Without filters, its 10 nearest are all from the story,

363
00:22:20,544 --> 00:22:24,627
距离从 0，也就是这个 chunk 自己，到 0.16
at distances from 0, the chunk itself, up to 0.16.

364
00:22:24,866 --> 00:22:26,276
加上代码里的过滤
With the code's filters,

365
00:22:26,276 --> 00:22:29,389
10 个结果全都来自 The Complete Book of Cheese
all 10 results come from The Complete Book of Cheese.

366
00:22:29,709 --> 00:22:34,210
它们的距离在 0.28 到 0.31 之间
Their distances run from 0.28 to 0.31.

367
00:22:34,530 --> 00:22:36,056
过滤先起作用
The filters act first,

368
00:22:36,056 --> 00:22:40,632
top K 再用剩下的东西填满 10 个位置，不管有多远
and top K fills its 10 places with whatever survives, however far.

369
00:22:40,866 --> 00:22:44,115
课上把元数据过滤放在排序之后
The lecture puts metadata filtering after ranking:

370
00:22:44,115 --> 00:22:48,077
放在这里，故事的 10 个 chunk 就会全部被丢掉，什么也不返回
here, that would drop all 10 story chunks and return nothing.

371
00:22:48,397 --> 00:22:52,322
Chroma 先过滤，所以你会拿到 10 个结果，讲的却是别的奶酪
Chroma filters first, so you get 10 results, about the wrong cheese.

372
00:22:52,566 --> 00:22:58,321
一个小疏漏：README 说有各种过滤，但只有第 4 种会运行
A small slip: the README promises various filters, but only variant 4 runs;

373
00:22:58,321 --> 00:23:00,929
第 1 到 3 种都被注释掉了
variants 1 to 3 are commented out.

374
00:23:01,249 --> 00:23:05,174
把第 1 种取消注释：不加过滤，每个 chunk 都来竞争
Uncomment the first, with no filter, and every chunk competes.

375
00:23:05,494 --> 00:23:08,972
还有，$contains 是关键词过滤，不是关键词排序
And $contains is a keyword filter, not a keyword ranking.

376
00:23:09,216 --> 00:23:11,828
重启后检查用的那条 --get 命令
The --get command from the restart check

377
00:23:11,828 --> 00:23:15,744
用了同样的按书过滤，但没有问题，所以也没有距离
uses the same book filter, but no question, so no distances.

378
00:23:16,064 --> 00:23:18,985
这 10 条记录，最前面是 Gutenberg 的开头声明
Its 10 records start with the Gutenberg header,

379
00:23:18,985 --> 00:23:21,035
接着是书名页和书的目录
then the title page and contents.

380
00:23:21,355 --> 00:23:24,129
这段声明，还有每本书结尾的许可证
That header, and each book's closing license,

381
00:23:24,129 --> 00:23:27,456
都会像普通文本一样被建进索引：先把它们去掉，再分块
are indexed like any text: strip them before chunking.

382
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:33,350
接下来是生成
Now generation.

383
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:36,215
课上最终的 prompt 有三部分
The lecture's final prompt has three parts:

384
00:23:36,215 --> 00:23:40,012
规定模型行为的 system prompt、用户的查询
a system prompt that says how to behave, the user's query,

385
00:23:40,012 --> 00:23:42,893
以及从数据库检索到的上下文
and the context retrieved from the database.

386
00:23:43,133 --> 00:23:45,275
到了 chat 这一步，代码再查询一次
In chat, the code queries again,

387
00:23:45,275 --> 00:23:48,019
这次不加过滤，要 10 个结果
this time with no filter, for 10 results.

388
00:23:48,417 --> 00:23:50,495
然后它拼出 input prompt
Then it builds the input prompt:

389
00:23:50,495 --> 00:23:54,390
先是问题，后面跟着 10 个 chunk，用换行符连起来
the question, followed by the 10 chunks, joined by newlines.

390
00:23:54,710 --> 00:23:57,846
这个 prompt 发给 gemini-3.1-flash-lite
The prompt goes to gemini-3.1-flash-lite.

391
00:23:58,083 --> 00:23:59,747
那 system prompt 在哪儿？
So where's the system prompt?

392
00:24:00,067 --> 00:24:03,237
第 40 行定义了一个：只根据 chunk 回答
Line 40 defines one: answer only from the chunks,

393
00:24:03,237 --> 00:24:05,955
chunk 里的信息不够时就直说
and say so when they don't contain enough.

394
00:24:06,275 --> 00:24:07,718
可是看看这次调用
But look at the call.

395
00:24:07,768 --> 00:24:09,117
它从来没被发出去
It's never sent.

396
00:24:09,167 --> 00:24:13,476
一个小疏漏，改一行就能修好：通过一个 config 参数把它传进去
A small slip, with a one-line fix: pass it in a config argument.

397
00:24:13,796 --> 00:24:15,994
更早的 pipenv 分支确实把它发出去了
The older pipenv branch did send it.

398
00:24:16,314 --> 00:24:21,263
没有它，README 承诺的有依据的回答就只能靠这些 chunk 了
Without it, the README's promise of grounded answers rests on the chunks alone.

399
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:24,465
再注意一下什么没变：模型本身
And notice what didn't change: the model itself.

400
00:24:24,785 --> 00:24:26,335
权重一个都没动
No weights moved.

401
00:24:26,385 --> 00:24:29,137
把 collection 删掉，这些知识就没了
Delete the collection, and the knowledge is gone.

402
00:24:29,383 --> 00:24:32,660
第 1 步和第 2 步：python cli.py --chat
Steps 1 and 2: python cli.py --chat,

403
00:24:32,660 --> 00:24:36,210
分别用 char-split 和 recursive-split
for char-split and for recursive-split.

404
00:24:36,530 --> 00:24:39,346
没有密钥，两条都停在把问题向量化这一步
Without a key, both stop embedding the question.

405
00:24:39,666 --> 00:24:43,634
每个问题要一次 embedding 调用，加一次 Gemini 调用
Each question costs one embedding call and one Gemini call.

406
00:24:43,883 --> 00:24:48,842
有密钥的话，要找的是查询，它打印出来带两个问号
With your key, look for the query, printed with two question marks,

407
00:24:48,842 --> 00:24:52,246
一个无害的小疏漏，还有它的 256 个 embedding 值
a harmless slip, and its 256 embedding values.

408
00:24:52,566 --> 00:24:55,395
然后是结果、数字 10、input prompt
Then the results, the number 10, the input prompt

409
00:24:55,395 --> 00:24:57,878
里面有你的 chunk，以及模型的回答
with your chunks, and the model's response.

410
00:24:59,117 --> 00:25:00,824
还记得开头那个问题吗？
Remember the opening question?

411
00:25:01,144 --> 00:25:02,446
这个故事是虚构的
The story is fiction,

412
00:25:02,446 --> 00:25:07,010
所以回答里讲到 Mara、她祖父和凝乳的内容，来自你的 chunk
so an answer about Mara, her grandfather and the curd came from your chunks.

413
00:25:07,330 --> 00:25:10,978
关于 Tolminc 的现实规定，来自模型的记忆
Real-world rules for Tolminc came from the model's memory.

414
00:25:11,298 --> 00:25:12,920
比较两种 chunk type 的结果
Compare both chunk types.

415
00:25:14,100 --> 00:25:17,513
第 3 步是一个链接，指向课程的对话工具，用 Chrome 打开
Step 3 is a link to the course's chat tool, in Chrome.

416
00:25:17,833 --> 00:25:18,833
暂停一下
Pause:

417
00:25:18,833 --> 00:25:21,716
用你的密钥，把两条 chat 命令都跑一遍，再试试这个工具
run both chat commands with your key, then try the tool.

418
00:25:22,036 --> 00:25:27,305
想问你自己的问题，就改 cli.py 的第 372 行
For your own question, change line 372 of cli.py.

419
00:25:30,650 --> 00:25:35,343
回到分块，看看课上最好的答案：在意思变化的地方切开
Back to chunking, with the lecture's best answer: cut where the meaning changes.

420
00:25:35,663 --> 00:25:39,271
在课件上，一个锚点沿着这些句子一路往前走
On the slides, an anchor walks through the sentences

421
00:25:39,271 --> 00:25:43,365
把相邻的句子并进来，前提是相似度保持在 0.8 以上
and joins neighbors while their similarity stays above 0.8.

422
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:46,843
代码用的是同样的材料，规则却不一样
The code uses the same ingredients with a different rule.

423
00:25:47,163 --> 00:25:51,511
每个句子都有一个窗口：它自己，加上两边各一个相邻的句子
Every sentence gets a window, itself and one neighbor on each side,

424
00:25:51,511 --> 00:25:53,328
每个窗口都要向量化
and each window is embedded.

425
00:25:53,567 --> 00:25:57,220
然后它量出每个窗口和下一个窗口之间的距离
Then it measures the distance between each window and the next,

426
00:25:57,220 --> 00:25:59,945
画在文本上方，就像地震仪一样
and plots it over the text, like a seismograph.

427
00:26:00,183 --> 00:26:05,580
接着它在第 95 百分位画一条线，在每个超过这条线的尖峰处切开
Next, it draws a line at the 95th percentile, and cuts at every spike above it.

428
00:26:05,900 --> 00:26:09,271
所以最大的那 5% 的落差，就成了 chunk 边界
So the biggest 5 percent of gaps become chunk boundaries.

429
00:26:09,517 --> 00:26:12,284
用 char-split 时，chunk 这一步没有密钥也跑通了
char-split ran the chunk step without a key.

430
00:26:12,376 --> 00:26:13,976
那 semantic-split 行吗？
Can semantic-split?

431
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:28,317
不行。要找出意思在哪里转折，它得先把每个句子窗口都向量化
No. To find where the meaning shifts, it has to embed every sentence window first.

432
00:26:28,637 --> 00:26:31,506
看看交给分块器的那个函数
Look at the function handed to the chunker:

433
00:26:31,506 --> 00:26:35,443
generate text embeddings，和 embed 这一步用的是同一个
generate_text_embeddings, the same one the embed step uses.

434
00:26:35,683 --> 00:26:40,291
README 里的命令，用 semantic-split 把三步一起跑
The README's command runs all three steps with --chunk_type semantic-split.

435
00:26:40,611 --> 00:26:43,474
在我们的机器上，它在 chunk 这一步里就失败了
On our machine it fails inside the chunk step,

436
00:26:43,474 --> 00:26:46,585
卡在第一本书，一个 chunk 都还没保存
on the first book, before a single chunk is saved.

437
00:26:46,833 --> 00:26:49,099
有密钥的话，先做好预算
With your key, budget for it:

438
00:26:49,099 --> 00:26:54,021
按我们的估算，给语料分块大约要 528 次 embedding 调用
by our estimate, about 528 embedding calls to chunk the corpus,

439
00:26:54,021 --> 00:26:58,396
向量化这些 chunk 还要大约 90 次，再加 10 到 20 分钟
about 90 more to embed the chunks, and 10 to 20 minutes.

440
00:26:58,716 --> 00:27:02,257
先只放一本书试试，再把其他的放回去，重新跑一遍
Try one book first, then put the others back and run it again.

441
00:27:02,577 --> 00:27:04,473
要找的是每本书的 chunk 数
Look for a chunk count per book,

442
00:27:04,473 --> 00:27:08,444
最后是插入 semantic-split-collection 完成的那一行
and finally, finished inserting into the semantic-split-collection.

443
00:27:08,683 --> 00:27:10,799
切出来的 chunk 长短很不均匀
The chunks come out very uneven,

444
00:27:10,799 --> 00:27:14,635
就连只讲一个主题的书，也会在它最大的几处落差上被切开
and even a single-topic book gets cut at its biggest gaps.

445
00:27:14,955 --> 00:27:17,942
之后再加一个额外步骤：chat 这一步也一样能用
Afterwards, an extra: chat works the same way.

446
00:27:18,262 --> 00:27:20,075
暂停一下，用你的密钥试试
Pause and try it, with your key.

447
00:27:23,417 --> 00:27:25,017
课上走得更远
The lecture goes further.

448
00:27:25,230 --> 00:27:29,433
它的框架加了一个检索前阶段和一个检索后阶段
Its frame adds a pre-retrieval stage and a post-retrieval stage.

449
00:27:29,753 --> 00:27:35,492
语义分块属于检索前：这是这个教程唯一实现了的进阶手段
Semantic chunking sits in pre-retrieval: the one advanced lever this tutorial implements.

450
00:27:35,812 --> 00:27:38,244
下面再讲三个，只讲思路
Here are three more, as ideas only.

451
00:27:38,484 --> 00:27:41,279
同样在检索之前：查询改写
Also before retrieval: query rewriting.

452
00:27:41,599 --> 00:27:46,527
用一个模型把杂乱的问题改写成干净的问题，比如“海豚住在哪里”
A model turns a cluttered question into a clean one, like where do dolphins live.

453
00:27:46,847 --> 00:27:50,516
但要是给它一个含糊的问题，改写可能会编造细节
But hand it a vague question, and the rewrite can invent details.

454
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:53,869
检索阶段：混合检索
In retrieval: hybrid search.

455
00:27:54,189 --> 00:27:58,008
关键词能锁定名字和罕见词；向量能抓住意思
Keywords pin down names and rare words; vectors catch meaning.

456
00:27:58,328 --> 00:27:59,728
拿这个问题来说
Take the question:

457
00:27:59,728 --> 00:28:02,505
Chester went to the bank of the river in the morning
Chester went to the bank of the river in the morning.

458
00:28:02,573 --> 00:28:04,920
两种方法给三个段落排出的顺序不一样
The two rank three paragraphs differently.

459
00:28:05,167 --> 00:28:09,929
倒数排名融合给每个段落记二分之一除以它的排名
Reciprocal rank fusion gives each paragraph one half divided by its rank,

460
00:28:09,929 --> 00:28:11,951
每个列表各记一次，再加起来
in each list, and adds them up.

461
00:28:12,271 --> 00:28:19,439
和问题几乎同义的那一段以 0.75 胜出，领先 0.67 和 0.42
The near paraphrase wins with 0.75, ahead of 0.67 and 0.42.

462
00:28:20,934 --> 00:28:23,025
检索之后：重排序
After retrieval: re-ranking.

463
00:28:23,345 --> 00:28:27,885
一个快速的检索器，向量在问题出现之前就做好了
A fast retriever, whose vectors were made before the question existed,

464
00:28:27,885 --> 00:28:31,259
它返回 25 个候选，对的那几个散落在其中
returns 25 candidates with the right ones scattered.

465
00:28:31,579 --> 00:28:35,888
再由一个更慢的模型，把问题和每个 chunk 放在一起读，重新排序
A slower model reads each question and chunk together and reorders them.

466
00:28:37,184 --> 00:28:39,573
这些都不在 cli.py 里
None of these is in cli.py.

467
00:28:39,893 --> 00:28:44,704
你会用上它们，是在朴素检索取回了错的 chunk 的时候
They're what you reach for when naive retrieval brings back the wrong chunks;

468
00:28:44,704 --> 00:28:47,829
而我们那个带过滤的查询，只需要把过滤去掉
our filtered query only needed its filter removed.

469
00:28:50,667 --> 00:28:52,267
该拆掉了
Time to tear down.

470
00:28:52,331 --> 00:28:56,068
输入 exit，再在 repo 目录里运行：docker compose down
Type exit, then docker compose down from the repo folder:

471
00:28:56,068 --> 00:29:00,331
还是那些无害的警告，然后 Chroma 和网络就没了
the same harmless warnings, then Chroma and the network are gone.

472
00:29:02,250 --> 00:29:03,750
这些 image 还在
The images stay:

473
00:29:03,750 --> 00:29:08,988
CLI 的 image 有 2.11 GB，包括它的 Python base image
2.11 gigabytes for the CLI image, its Python base included,

474
00:29:08,988 --> 00:29:11,594
Chroma 的有 826 MB
and 826 megabytes for Chroma.

475
00:29:11,834 --> 00:29:16,101
现在 git status 只显示你对 docker-shell.sh 的改动
Now git status shows only your edit to docker-shell.sh.

476
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:19,541
而 outputs 和 docker-volumes 两个目录都被忽略
The outputs/ and docker-volumes/ folders are ignored,

477
00:29:19,541 --> 00:29:21,034
留在你的磁盘上
and stay on your disk.

478
00:29:21,084 --> 00:29:23,388
Google Cloud 上没有任何东西一直在运行
Nothing keeps running in Google Cloud;

479
00:29:23,388 --> 00:29:25,329
你只为发送过的内容付了费
you paid only for what you sent.

480
00:29:25,649 --> 00:29:27,479
把密钥放在 repo 旁边
Keep the key beside the repo:

481
00:29:27,479 --> 00:29:31,772
放在里面的话，git 不会忽略它，image 也会把它复制进去
inside it, git wouldn't ignore the key, and the image would copy it.

482
00:29:32,092 --> 00:29:33,692
课程结束后，把它删掉
Delete it when the course ends.

483
00:29:34,012 --> 00:29:38,065
现在就暂停，把它拆掉，这样下次 port 8000 就是空着的
Pause and tear down now, so port 8000 is free next time.

484
00:29:40,300 --> 00:29:44,908
最后一个教训，来自课程团队留下的下节课 agent 的运行记录
One last lesson, from the staff's recorded run of next lecture's agent.

485
00:29:45,228 --> 00:29:47,461
它检索到的是讲转场放牧的文本
It retrieved text about transhumance

486
00:29:47,461 --> 00:29:50,625
来自一本更早的 Tolminc 书，当天就被换掉了
from an older Tolminc book, replaced that same day.

487
00:29:50,945 --> 00:29:56,002
数据库只根据加载进去的内容回答：书一变，就要重建索引
The database answers from what was loaded: when the books change, rebuild the index.

488
00:29:56,250 --> 00:29:59,130
下节课会用一个 agent 来跑这条命令
Next lecture runs this command with an agent.

489
00:29:59,450 --> 00:30:03,269
在课程团队的那次运行里，模型自己选了要调用哪个检索工具
In the staff's run, the model chose which retrieval tool to call.

490
00:30:03,589 --> 00:30:05,793
课上讲的 Self-RAG 走得更远
The lecture's Self-RAG goes further:

491
00:30:05,793 --> 00:30:10,202
由模型决定到底要不要检索，然后再检查它找到的东西
the model decides whether to retrieve at all, then checks what it found.

492
00:30:10,522 --> 00:30:14,128
我们的 chat 每个问题都要翻书，而且什么都不检查
Our chat opens the book for every question, and checks nothing.

493
00:30:15,367 --> 00:30:16,967
那四个问题呢？
And the four questions?

494
00:30:17,095 --> 00:30:19,527
所谓 embedding，就是表示意思的一个方向
An embedding is a direction for meaning.

495
00:30:19,847 --> 00:30:23,559
向量数据库存的是记录，再用一个索引来搜索它们
A vector database stores records, with an index to search them.

496
00:30:23,879 --> 00:30:26,631
查询找的是问题的最近邻
A query finds the question's nearest neighbors.

497
00:30:26,951 --> 00:30:30,130
上下文，就是你贴进 prompt 里的那些 chunk
The context is the chunks you paste into the prompt.

498
00:30:30,367 --> 00:30:32,372
五道题，自测一下
Five questions to test yourself.

499
00:30:32,692 --> 00:30:36,874
第一题：哪些参数属于哪条通道，两条通道又必须共用什么？
One: which flags belong to each lane, and what must both lanes share?

500
00:30:37,194 --> 00:30:41,128
第二题：为什么 CLI 按名字就能找到数据库
Two: why does the CLI reach the database by name,

501
00:30:41,128 --> 00:30:42,975
又是谁在用 port 8000？
and who uses port 8000?

502
00:30:43,217 --> 00:30:45,542
第三题：重叠有什么好处，又有什么代价？
Three: what does overlap buy and cost?

503
00:30:45,862 --> 00:30:48,828
还有，为什么递归切分器切出了更多 chunk？
And why did the recursive splitter make more chunks?

504
00:30:49,148 --> 00:30:52,796
第四题：README 里的查询为什么没返回任何 Tolminc 文本？
Four: why did the README's query return no Tolminc text?

505
00:30:53,116 --> 00:30:56,230
第五题：这个 prompt 少了什么，又该怎么修？
Five: what is the prompt missing, and what's the fix?

506
00:30:56,467 --> 00:31:01,650
答案在练习里，每条命令都在学习指南里
The answers are in the exercises, and every command is in the study guide,

507
00:31:01,650 --> 00:31:03,550
就在 MLOps Learning 这个 repo 里
in the MLOps Learning repo.

508
00:31:03,870 --> 00:31:05,491
下节课：agent
Next time: agents.
